WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.673
Chicken Little

00:00:02.373 --> 00:00:07.025
One day Henny-penny was picking up corn in the rickyard under the big oak tree.

00:00:07.675 --> 00:00:08.484
Whack!

00:00:08.834 --> 00:00:10.897
An acorn hit her upon the head.

00:00:11.247 --> 00:00:13.809
"Goodness gracious me!" said Henny-penny.

00:00:14.159 --> 00:00:17.819
"The sky's a-going to fall; I must go and tell the King."

00:00:18.469 --> 00:00:23.837
So she went along, and she went along, and she went along, crying, "The sky's a-falling!

00:00:24.187 --> 00:00:25.739
The sky's a-falling!"

00:00:26.389 --> 00:00:28.142
Till she met Cocky-locky.

00:00:28.492 --> 00:00:31.663
"Where are you going, Henny-penny?" says Cocky-locky.

00:00:32.013 --> 00:00:32.875
"Oh!

00:00:33.225 --> 00:00:37.035
I'm going to tell the King the sky's a-falling," says Henny-penny.

00:00:37.385 --> 00:00:40.085
"May I come with you?" says Cocky-locky.

00:00:40.435 --> 00:00:42.454
"Certainly," says Henny-penny.

00:00:43.104 --> 00:00:46.592
They went along, and they went along, till they met Ducky-daddles.

00:00:46.942 --> 00:00:47.804
"Oh!

00:00:48.154 --> 00:00:53.255
we're going to tell the King the sky's a-falling," said Henny-penny and Cocky-locky.

00:00:53.605 --> 00:00:56.313
"May I come with you?" says Ducky-daddles.

00:00:56.663 --> 00:00:59.387
"Certainly," said Henny-penny and Cocky-locky.

00:01:00.037 --> 00:01:03.582
They went along, and they went along, till they met Goosey-poosey.

00:01:03.932 --> 00:01:04.794
"Oh!

00:01:05.144 --> 00:01:11.401
we're going to tell the King the sky's a-falling," said Henny-penny, Cocky-locky, and Ducky-daddles.

00:01:11.751 --> 00:01:14.440
"May I come with you?" said Goosey-poosey.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.457
"Certainly," they said.

00:01:17.107 --> 00:01:20.578
They went along, and they went along, till they met Turkey-lurkey.

00:01:20.928 --> 00:01:23.616
"May I come with you?" said Turkey-lurkey.

00:01:23.966 --> 00:01:29.123
"Oh, certainly," said Henny-penny, Cocky-locky, Ducky-daddles, and Goosey-poosey.

00:01:29.773 --> 00:01:33.372
They went along, and they went along, till they met Foxy-woxy.

00:01:33.722 --> 00:01:34.584
"Oh!

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:38.360
but this is not the way to the King," says Foxy-woxy.

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:44.672
"I know the proper way; shall I show it you?" "Oh, certainly, Foxy-woxy," said they all.

00:01:45.322 --> 00:01:49.963
So they went along, and they went along, till they came to a narrow and dark hole.

00:01:50.313 --> 00:01:53.090
This was the door of Foxy-woxy's burrow.

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:57.484
"This is the short cut to the King's palace," said Foxy-woxy.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:58.986
"Follow me!"

00:01:59.636 --> 00:02:03.990
So Foxy-woxy slipped into the dark burrow, and turned round to wait.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:08.736
Now Turkey-lurkey was the first to go through the dark hole into the burrow.

00:02:09.386 --> 00:02:14.806
He hadn't got far when — "Hrumph!" Foxy-woxy snapped off Turkey-lurkey's head.

00:02:15.156 --> 00:02:21.325
Then Goosey-poosey went in, and — "Hrumph!" Then Ducky-daddles waddled down, and — "Hrumph!"

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:24.880
Then Cocky-locky strutted down into the burrow.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:32.748
But Cocky-locky will always crow whether you want him to do so or not, and so he had just time for one "Cock-a-doodle-doo!"

00:02:33.398 --> 00:02:41.153
Now when Henny-penny, who had just got into the dark burrow, heard Cocky-locky crow, she said to herself: "My goodness!

00:02:41.503 --> 00:02:42.822
It must be dawn.

00:02:43.172 --> 00:02:47.971
Time for me to lay my egg." So she turned round and bustled off to her nest.

00:02:48.621 --> 00:02:52.376
So she escaped — but she never told the King the sky was falling!

00:02:53.026 --> 00:02:55.921
After all, the sky was never falling at all.

00:02:56.271 --> 00:02:58.184
It was only ever an acorn.

00:02:58.534 --> 00:02:59.516
The end.

